-- Section 1: Scaling Efficiency --

  Run a fixed per-GPU workload at 1/2/4/8 GPUs. Efficiency = speedup / N.
  Ideal is a straight line (eff 1.0); the gap is communication overhead.

   GPUs    tok/s   speedup  efficiency
      1      100     1.00x       1.00
      2      191     1.91x       0.95
      4      364     3.64x       0.91
      8      656     6.56x       0.82
  [check] 8-GPU efficiency >= 0.80

-- Section 2: NCCL Communication Cost --

  The scaling curve usually bends at the node boundary because intra-node NVLink
  is ~10x faster than inter-node InfiniBand for the same collective.

  AllReduce 1.3GB across 8 GPUs:
    NVLink ~600 GB/s :    3.79 ms
    InfiniBand ~50   :   45.50 ms  (12x slower)
  [check] inter-node collective is the likely 4->8 GPU efficiency drop

-- Section 3: Amdahl Speedup Ceiling --

  Non-overlapped communication is a serial fraction s. Amdahl caps speedup at
  1 / (s + (1-s)/N), no matter how many GPUs you add.

  serial fraction 2%: 8-GPU ceiling = 7.02x, infinite-GPU ceiling = 50.0x
  serial fraction 5%: 8-GPU ceiling = 5.93x, infinite-GPU ceiling = 20.0x
  serial fraction 10%: 8-GPU ceiling = 4.71x, infinite-GPU ceiling = 10.0x
  [check] smaller serial fraction => higher achievable speedup

